We prove the integral scalar-curvature inequality proposed by Gromov. For every dimension n ≥ 3, there is a constant $a_n\gt 0$, depending only on n, such that $\displaystyle \int_M(\mathop{\mathrm{Scal}}
olimits _g^-)^{n/2}\,dV_g\ge a_n\|M\|$ for every closed connected oriented smooth n-manifold M and every smooth Riemannian metric g. Here $\mathop{\mathrm{Scal}}
olimits _g^-:=\max\{0,-\mathop{\mathrm{Scal}}
olimits _g\}$, and $\|M\|$ is real simplicial volume. The proof uses the nonnegative-scalar-curvature vanishing theorem of the companion paper on rational inessentiality.

